    - target: {fileID: 6668015293666917239, guid: d7425ed2047e64d8ea6ff79f20bd46f6, type: 3}
      propertyPath: HelpText
      value: "This scene shows how to lock the camera onto a nearby target.  There
        are two Cinemachine Cameras in the scene: Orbital Follow and Follow with
        Lock On Boss.\n\nThe Orbital Follow is a simple 3rd Person View camera that
        is following and looking at the player while having the ability to rotate
        around the player using the mouse.\n\nFollow with Lock On Boss is also a
        3rd Person View camera. However, this one is following the an invisible GameObject
        (FollowTarget) on the player, while looking at the boss. The invisible GameObject
        is always rotated on the Y axis so it looks towards the boss. This is achieved
        with the Look At Target script on FollowTarget.\n\nThe switch between the
        two Cinemachine Cameras happens when the player moves close to the boss.
        This is done using Cinemachine Trigger Action. This proximity is visualized
        in the scene with a transparent cylinder around the boss - see Proximity
        Trigger GameObject.\n\nUse WASD to move around, Spacebar to jump, Shift to
        sprint.  Mouse moves the camera. \nIf using Input package, right mouse button
        to jump and middle mouse button to sprint."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 9138370430051789472, guid: d7425ed2047e64d8ea6ff79f20bd46f6, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Name
      value: HelpUI
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
